  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "116",
  "quote": "A landlord shall not increase the rent charged to a tenant for a rental unit without first giving the tenant at least 90 days written notice of the landlord’s intention to do so.",
  "reason": "The clause is consistent with Section 116 of the Act, which requires the landlord to give at least 90 days' written notice of a rent increase in a form approved by the Board setting out the new rent. Because it complies with the Act rather than conflicting with it, it is not made void by Section 4."
}

